Rollback Verification Tests (SRE Validation)

A rollback is only successful if the endpoint is both restored and functional. After automatic rollback completes, execute the following verification suite.


1. Verify Endpoint Config Reverted

Capture the active EndpointConfig:

CURRENT_CONFIG=$(aws sagemaker describe-endpoint \
  --endpoint-name my-endpoint \
  --query EndpointConfigName \
  --output text)

echo "Current Config: $CURRENT_CONFIG"

Compare against the expected rollback target:

Shell

EXPECTED_CONFIG=$(cat previous_config.txt)

if [ "$CURRENT_CONFIG" != "$EXPECTED_CONFIG" ]; then
    echo "FAIL: Rollback config mismatch"
    exit 1
fi

echo "PASS: Correct config restored"

Check
 EndpointConfig matches rollback target
 Failed configuration no longer active


2. Verify Endpoint Returns to InService
STATUS=$(aws sagemaker describe-endpoint \
  --endpoint-name my-endpoint \
  --query EndpointStatus \
  --output text)

echo "$STATUS"



Expected:
InService


